.\" Manual page for exifrename.py. Keep in sync with README.md and "exifrename.py --help".
.TH EXIFRENAME.PY 1 "2026-10-29" "exifrename.py 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
exifrename.py \- rename or copy image files after their EXIF date
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B exifrename.py
.RB [ \-c ]
.RB [ \-r ]
.RB [ \-m
.IR MASK ]
.RB [ \-f ]
.RB [ \-\-copy
.RI [ FOLDER ]]
.RB [ \-\-copytree
.IR FOLDER ]
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.RB [ \-l
.RI [ FILE ]]
.RB [ \-\-doubtful\-count
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-doubtful\-seconds
.IR S ]
.RI [ PATTERN " ...]"
.br
.B exifrename.py
.B \-u
.RB [ \-r ]
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.RI [ PATTERN " ...]"
.br
.B exifrename.py
.RB ( \-\-check " | " \-v " | " \-h )
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B exifrename.py
names image files after the date they were taken, read from EXIF, using a mask.
A file whose EXIF date is not trustworthy is skipped unless
.B \-f
is given.
The validity rules are those of
.BR metadata.py .
Every rename is recorded in
.B exifrename.map
in the folder of the file so that it can be undone with
.BR \-u .
Switches are case-insensitive.
One of
.IR PATTERN ,
.B \-c
or
.B \-r
is required.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I PATTERN
File names or wildcards, matched case-insensitively.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-current
All image files in the current folder.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-recursive
Include subfolders. With a PATTERN, select matching files in every subfolder.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mask " \fIMASK\fR"
New name, default \fBEXIF\-%YYYY%\-%MM%\-%DD%_%HH%\-%II%\-%SS%\fR.
Tags: %YYYY% %YY% (year), %MMMMMM% %MMMM% (month name, full and short, English),
%MM% (month), %DD% (day), %HH% (24\-hour), %HHHH% (12\-hour, am/pm added),
%II% (minutes), %SS% (seconds), %file% (original name without extension),
%folder% (folder name), %% (a literal %). The extension is kept.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Rename even if the EXIF date is invalid, using the EXIF save date, the GPS date stamp,
or the file creation/modification time, in that order.
.TP
.BR \-\-copy " [\fIFOLDER\fR]"
Copy instead of rename. Copies go to FOLDER, or beside the originals.
.TP
.BR \-\-copytree " \fIFOLDER\fR"
Like \-\-copy, but recreate the folder tree relative to the current folder below FOLDER.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-undo
Restore old names from exifrename.map (current folder, or all subfolders with \-r).
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Show what would happen; change nothing.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-log " [\fIFILE\fR]"
Also write the output to a log (default exifrename.log, appended).
.TP
.BI \-\-doubtful\-count " N"
Mark EXIF dates doubtful when a folder has more than N images within
\-\-doubtful\-seconds of each other (default 20; 0 turns it off).
.TP
.BI \-\-doubtful\-seconds " S"
Time span for the doubtful check (default 60).
.TP
.B \-\-check
Check prerequisites (Pillow) and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-? ", " \-\-help
Show help.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B exifrename.map
CSV (new_name,old_name) per folder.
.TP
.B exifrename.log
Default log file.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success, 1 error or nothing found, 2 usage error, 130 interrupted.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR metadata.py (1)
